// A name in a sequence pattern is a binding for that element
// (spec/04-semantics.md, match Expression, "Class patterns": a bare name in
// brackets is a binding). This is so also when a global class has the
// same name: the arm binds the element, and does not test it against the
// class.
class Shape {}

print match [1, 2] {
    case [Shape, b] => "elem " + str(Shape) + " " + str(b)
    case _ => "no match"
};

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: elem 1 2
